<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <OutputType>Library</OutputType>
    <SolutionDir Condition="$(SolutionDir) == '' Or $(SolutionDir) == '*Undefined*'">..\..\</SolutionDir>
    <GenerateAssemblyInfo>false</GenerateAssemblyInfo>
    <CodeAnalysisRuleSet>AllRules.ruleset</CodeAnalysisRuleSet>
    <!--
      A portable target framework, and no WinForms. This is the point the whole of Phase 1 has been
      walking towards: MediaPortal.Common is the assembly the server, the database layer and (in
      Phase 2) the Avalonia frontend all reference, so as long as it carried -windows everything
      above it did too, and CA1416 had nothing to say about it.

      Getting here is what the last several steps were for, each one removing a hard Windows
      dependency rather than papering over it: System.Management (WMI disk/CPU queries -> DriveInfo
      and /proc/cpuinfo), System.ServiceProcess.ServiceController plus the power handling and the
      WM_POWERBROADCAST window (all three classes moved to MediaPortal.Common.Windows behind
      ISystemStateService), Dokan behind IResourceMountingService, LogonUser impersonation behind
      IImpersonationService, GDI+ behind IImageTransformer, and the Kernel32 waitable timer behind
      ITaskWakeUpTimer. What is left is registry access that is guarded by OperatingSystem.IsWindows(),
      which is why CA1416 is an error below: the analyzer's judgement of this assembly is now
      trustworthy enough to gate on.

      UseWindowsForms is not set at all rather than set to false. Nothing in this project names a
      WinForms type any more (Application.ExecutablePath and SystemInformation.Network became
      Environment and NetworkInterface on the way here), and the SDK refuses the combination:
      UseWindowsForms=true needs a -windows target framework, which is exactly the constraint being
      lifted.
    -->
    <WarningsAsErrors>CA1416</WarningsAsErrors>
  </PropertyGroup>
  <PropertyGroup>
    <!--required for assemblies from nuget packages to be copied to output folder, so our build.targets can copy them further -->
    <CopyLocalLockFileAssemblies>true</CopyLocalLockFileAssemblies>
  </PropertyGroup>
  <PropertyGroup Condition=" '$(Configuration)|$(Platform)' == 'Debug|x86' ">
    <OutputPath>bin\x86\Debug\</OutputPath>
    <CodeAnalysisRuleSet>AllRules.ruleset</CodeAnalysisRuleSet>
  </PropertyGroup>
  <PropertyGroup Condition=" '$(Configuration)|$(Platform)' == 'Release|x86' ">
    <OutputPath>bin\x86\Release\</OutputPath>
    <DebugType>none</DebugType>
    <CodeAnalysisRuleSet>AllRules.ruleset</CodeAnalysisRuleSet>
  </PropertyGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\MediaPortal.Utilities\MediaPortal.Utilities.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\UPnP\UPnP.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <None Update="build.targets">
      <SubType>Designer</SubType>
    </None>
  </ItemGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="DuoVia.FuzzyStrings">
      <Version>2.1.0</Version>
    </PackageReference>
    <PackageReference Include="Newtonsoft.Json">
      <Version>13.0.1</Version>
    </PackageReference>
    <!--
      Two Windows-oriented packages used to sit here; both are gone now, and every one of them that
      leaves the core is one fewer thing to re-home when this project stops targeting Windows.

      System.Management had exactly one consumer, CrashLoggerBase's drive enumeration, which now
      uses System.IO.DriveInfo.

      System.ServiceProcess.ServiceController looked unused - nothing mentions ServiceController -
      but it was not dead: SystemStateService and PowerEventHandler used PowerBroadcastStatus, whose
      .NET implementation ships in that package. Both classes now live in
      MediaPortal.Common.Windows, which references the package itself. A dependency that hides
      behind an enum name is worth remembering when grepping package names "proves" one unused.
    -->
    <PackageReference Include="System.Runtime.Caching" Version="6.0.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="System.Threading.Tasks.Dataflow" Version="6.0.0" />
  </ItemGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="log4net" Version="3.5.0" />
  </ItemGroup>
  <ItemGroup Condition="'$(TargetFrameworkIdentifier)' == '.NETFramework'">
    <Reference Include="System.Web" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.AspNet.WebApi.Owin">
      <Version>5.2.7</Version>
    </PackageReference>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Owin.Security.OAuth">
      <Version>4.0.1</Version>
    </PackageReference>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Owin">
      <Version>4.1.0</Version>
    </PackageReference>
  </ItemGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <Compile Remove="MediaManagement\MLQueries\CertificationAgeFilter.cs" />
    <Compile Remove="Services\MediaManagement\ImportDataflowBlocks\ChangeUnfoldBlock.cs" />
  </ItemGroup>
  <Import Project="build.targets" />
</Project>
